sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-03, single-swamp-node, rules 14-25.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:create
  %% kind: route.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Route Nodes<br/>workload · Router
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>private DNS
  CLI->>GW: route:create 12 shop.test
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve domain<br/>Route 14 pending · task #5120
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-route-create
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5120
  SW->>N: Make a CSR on the Node<br/>openssl req · key stays on Node
  SW->>GW: Sign the CSR<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
  %%> The Orbit CA key stays in the Gateway.
  GW-->>SW: Signed certificate
  opt Cluster-scoped Route
    SW->>N: Allow the Router on LAN<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall
    %%> The Router reaches workloads over LAN; there is no WireGuard fallback.
  end
  SW->>N: Install cert, publish site<br/>child route-create-site · reload
  %%> A validation error stops the reload; the written candidate stays for convergence.
  SW->>N: Probe the site over TLS<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · SNI shop.test
  %%> Runs from 209; an HTTP 500 does not fail the TLS check.
  opt --publication=public
    SW->>N: Open the Ingress edge<br/>Ingress Caddy · ufw 80/443
    %%> Public DNS is operator-managed. Caddy retries Let's Encrypt by itself.
  end
  opt domain outside the TLD
    SW->>V: Publish private DNS<br/>records + catalog, then restart
    %%> DNS goes last. Inside the TLD, private DNS already answers the whole zone.
    %%> dnsmasq reads records only at startup.
  end
  alt every step succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event + outputs
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Route 14 active · task succeeded
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the Route failed<br/>domain kept · rerun after a fix
    %%> There is no rollback. Rerun to converge, or route:destroy to remove what was added.
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5120
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
